    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d701">

                <pb facs="0808" n="696" xml:id="pg696"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13277: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Josselyn</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-14T16:00:00+08:00">November 14, 1935—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 14—3:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>58. Peiping’s November 13, 2 p.m.,<anchor n="18" xml:id="d701-f1"/> and my
                    November 13, 4 p.m. Yachow missionaries have arrived in Kiating. I telegraphed
                    yesterday to Tatsienlu but have not yet received a reply; the Hankow telegraph
                    office reported the wire open. Repeated to Peiping, Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josselyn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
